    "created_at": "2025-03-04T07:11:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-03-04T08:59:31Z",
    "body": "Hmm, maybe we don't have to filter out no-cors cases? Instead, we'd check ok-status only if the response is not opaque filtered response. If the response is a opaque filtered response, we may want to check response [type](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response-type) to check whether there is a network error or not instead.\r\n\r\nI wonder if updating this line\r\n\r\n> If raceNetworkRequestResponse’s [status](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response-status) is [ok status](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#ok-status), then:\r\n\r\nto \r\n\r\n> If raceNetworkRequestResponse’s [status](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response-status) is [ok status](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#ok-status), or (raceNetworkRequestResponse’s [type](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response-type) AND request [mode](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-request-mode) is \"no-cors\") then:\r\n\r\nmakes more sense to handle filtered response appropriately.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
